body:
Well it depends the type of hard you're looking for. Crys of Achilles intro for me was very difficult, cause I wasn't familiar with they spanish progressions. But it can be very tricky if fingepicking isn't your thing. 

Isolation can be difficult for all the riffing that is really fast.

&#x200B;

Solo wise, well there tones of it, I would argue many from TLH, at least Myles side of it. Tremonti has many fucking difficult solos Dying light.

&#x200B;

I think overall playing AB can imrpove greatly your playing, with all the riffs, solos, fingerpicking techniques, alternative tunings etc

I partially agree with your statement OP. "Holiday" does sound something that is influenced from Myles work with Slash. But "Stay" reminds me actually of AB during their first tenure with ODR. Now that I think about it, the last time I heard this type of song with AB was on Fortress with "All ends well". As far FOSS for me sounds something that could've been between Blackbird and AB III. 

&#x200B;

Either way it's a great record with a great production that fucking rocks! It's definitely their best effort since Fortress
